+# Working with Rojo day to day
+
+Git is the source of truth for this game. Code lives in files under `src/`, and `rojo serve` syncs
+those files into **your own dev place** in Studio. Studio is where you read, run, test, and
+playtest. You don't edit there. The README's Layout table shows where each folder lands in the
+place.
+
+## First-time setup
+
+1. Install the tools with `rokit install`, and the packages with `pesde install` (run it in the
+   repo root and in `test_packages/`).
+2. Make a dev place of your own in Studio. Don't use a shared, staging, or live place.
+3. Add your dev place's id to `servePlaceIds` in `default.project.json`. Rojo then won't
+   live-sync into any other place, so connecting to the wrong place by mistake can't overwrite
+   it. Commit that line in its own small change.
+4. Run `rojo serve` from the repo root (port 34872), open your dev place, and click **Connect**
+   in the Rojo plugin.
+
+## Where changes go
+
+- **Scripts and modules:** edit the files under `src/` in your editor. If you edit a script in
+  Studio, the next sync overwrites it and Git never sees the change.
+  - Server code goes in `src/ServerScriptService`.
+  - Code shared by the server and client goes in `src/ReplicatedStorage/Shared`.
+  - Client code goes in `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts`.
+  - UI goes in `src/StarterGui`.
+  - Specs go in `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs`, named `Name.spec.luau`.
+- **File names set the script type:** `*.server.luau` is a Script, `*.client.luau` is a
+  LocalScript, and any other `.luau` file is a ModuleScript.
+- **Attributes, tags, and properties:** put them in a `Name.meta.json` beside the file, or an
+  `init.meta.json` in the folder, using real JSON values (`true`, not `"true"`). Don't set them
+  in the Properties panel.
+- **Packages:** add them to `pesde.toml` (or `test_packages/pesde.toml` for test-only packages)
+  and run `pesde install`. Never edit anything in `roblox_packages/`. Require a package through
+  its link (`ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Vide`), never through a `.pesde/...` path.
+- **Things you have to build in Studio** (a model, a GUI): export them over their `.rbxm` file
+  with **Save to File**, or the next sync replaces them. For a whole session of Studio work, ask
+  before running `rojo syncback`, and read the whole diff afterwards.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **Rojo is still running.** Rojo 7.7.x can crash when you delete, move, or rename a file or
+  folder while it serves. Studio then quietly stops getting changes. After a delete, move, or
+  rename, check the terminal for `Rojo crashed!`. If it crashed, restart `rojo serve` and click
+  Connect again.
+- **Your edit actually arrived.** Before you trust a playtest or spec run, open the script in
+  Studio and confirm your new code is there. An error line number that didn't move with your edit
+  means Studio is running the old code.
+- **The right code is being served.** Studio runs whatever branch is checked out in the folder
+  where `rojo serve` started. A merged pull request does nothing until you pull it.
+- **Stop `rojo serve` first** before `git checkout`, `switch`, `pull`, `rebase`, `reset`,
+  `stash`, `pesde install`, or a bulk delete. Restart it afterwards.
+- **For a second branch at the same time,** use a `git worktree`, run `pesde install` in it, and
+  start its own server with `rojo serve --port <another port>`. Point a separate Studio window at
+  that port.
+- **Before you push,** run the checks in the README. `git status` should list only the files you
+  meant to change.
+
+## Keeping `default.project.json` healthy
+
+This file decides where every folder lands in the place. A bad merge in it breaks syncing,
+sourcemaps, and Jest for everyone.
+
+- **Most changes don't need it.** A new file inside an existing mapped folder syncs on its own.
+  Change the project file only for a new top-level mount, and update the README's Layout table in
+  the same commit.
+- **Resolving a conflict in it:** don't just pick one side. Keep both sides' intent, then compare
+  the result against the README's Layout table one row at a time. Watch for these:
+  - Every `$path` must point at a folder that exists. A typo such as `StarterPlayerScript` fails
+    the sourcemap.
+  - The Jest packages mount at `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`. Jest looks for them there,
+    not in `ReplicatedStorage`.
+  - Keep `globIgnorePaths: ["src/ServerScriptService/Tests"]`. `src/ServerScriptService` is
+    mounted whole, and `Tests` is mounted again on its own so its `Packages` child can be added.
+    Without the ignore, the place gets two `Tests` folders.
+- **Save it as UTF-8 without a byte order mark (BOM).** Rojo fails with "Failed to parse JSONC"
+  if the file starts with one. Windows PowerShell's `Set-Content` and `Out-File` add a BOM, and
+  some editors keep an existing BOM when they save. To check, run
+  `head -c 3 default.project.json | od -An -tx1` in Git Bash. The output must not be `ef bb bf`.
+- **Check it before you commit:** run
+  `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts` and then the
+  README's `luau-lsp analyze` command. If the sourcemap fails or the analysis can't resolve a
+  require, the mapping is wrong.
